## Anti Pattern

- [ ] **Security as Afterthought**: Add security at the end
- [ ] **Trusting User Input**: Without validation
- [ ] **Rolling Own Crypto**: Don't implement custom encryption
- [ ] **Hardcoded Secrets**: Store in code
- [ ] **Verbose Errors**: Leak internal details
- [ ] **Weak Passwords**: Allow simple passwords
- [ ] **No Logging**: Can't detect attacks
- [ ] **Single Layer Defense**: Rely on one security control

## Best Practice

- [ ] **Defense in Depth**: Multiple security layers
- [ ] **Principle of Least Privilege**: Minimal permissions
- [ ] **Fail Securely**: Default to deny
- [ ] **Input Validation**: Validate all inputs
- [ ] **Secure Defaults**: Start secure, relax intentionally
- [ ] **Regular Audits**: Continuous security review
- [ ] **Security Training**: Team awareness
- [ ] **Incident Response**: Plan for breaches

